            "matched_surface": "classification problems",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_66391fd4e0f078f48ee10db7",
            "source_text": "While we attacked regression problems by trying\nto minimize the squared error loss function,\nthe common loss function for classification problems is called *cross-entropy*,\nwhose name can be demystified \nvia an introduction to information theory in subsequent chapters.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_introduction_index_b069",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_introduction",
            "content_sha256": "f8f1ed7021eb82c8b2e28e17fbc4c33c16980d475d04712640785578bfde5c1b",
            "context_id": "ctx_18f207162816691afd0ac11d",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "classification problems",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_a555018c61a684de6955366a",
            "source_text": "Auto-tagging problems are typically best described\nas multi-label classification problems.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_introduction_index_b066",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_introduction",
            "content_sha256": "9fa7e10b0b1608471d553fd295d4f0df888b6a9f85a0597f8ab9f58f377a3549",
            "context_id": "ctx_275c69012387f631509a7b14",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "classification problems",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_0c7bde51b2948c01df8665d8",
            "source_text": "Some classification problems fit neatly\ninto the binary or multiclass classification setups.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_linear_networks_softmax_regression_b010",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_linear_networks",
            "content_sha256": "c404ea073b00e020404e09ac88265be1bdd3fb04e882442a85a211ff284d684e",
            "context_id": "ctx_4f3feaf3fe5fc9145ebc21e9",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "classification problems",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_3e2dceee6e0300a05d1b6868",
            "source_text": "But general classification problems do not come with natural orderings among the classes.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_mlp_b050",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
